00:36:49.124 --> 00:36:51.793
And they're able to literally
see every single atom as they

00:36:51.793 --> 00:36:53.995
break apart the particle.

00:36:53.995 --> 00:36:55.430
By just throwing
electrons at it,

00:36:55.430 --> 00:36:57.799
they say, the transmission
electron microscope

00:36:57.799 --> 00:37:00.302
was designed to break records.

00:37:00.302 --> 00:37:01.937
Using its beam of
electrons, scientists

00:37:01.937 --> 00:37:04.372
have glimpsed many types of
viruses, et cetera, et cetera.

00:37:04.372 --> 00:37:08.910
They got down to 0.4 angstrom
resolution in that work.

00:37:08.910 --> 00:37:10.045
It's a beautiful thing.

00:37:10.045 --> 00:37:12.013
And being able to
see these materials

00:37:12.013 --> 00:37:15.750
has revolutionized what
we can do with them.

00:37:15.750 --> 00:37:19.788
Diamonds and graphite makes
me, when I talk about graphite,

00:37:19.788 --> 00:37:21.790
I get excited.

00:37:21.790 --> 00:37:22.657
I get excited.

00:37:22.657 --> 00:37:25.026
Now I'm working on my arm here.

00:37:25.026 --> 00:37:28.330
So I got to go up that way.

00:37:28.330 --> 00:37:29.764
And I got to go this way.

00:37:35.570 --> 00:37:40.242
All right, hold on, hold
